# The PolicyHash is sha256 over a policy file's raw bytes. A checkout that
# converts line endings therefore changes the identity of a policy without
# changing the policy, and the generator embeds that hash into the code it
# emits. Committing this file is what makes a checkout byte-identical on every
# platform, so generation is reproducible and a hash means the same thing to
# every operator.
#
# This was found by TestFuzzSubjectMatchesGenerator: the committed subject
# carried a hash of CRLF bytes and CI, checking out LF, computed a different
# one.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
